1
00:00:01,065 --> 00:00:02,905
Well, my family has a mystical lineage.

2
00:00:02,985 --> 00:00:05,345
Remember that I'll always be by your side.

3
00:00:05,425 --> 00:00:06,785
From now on, let's be "F."

4
00:00:06,865 --> 00:00:08,345
Friends with benefits.

5
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:09,345
Thank you.

6
00:00:09,425 --> 00:00:12,345
I only made it through the difficult time
because of you.

7
00:00:12,425 --> 00:00:15,065
I think we can officially be
in the talking stage now.

8
00:00:15,665 --> 00:00:17,185
You don't need to win me over anymore.

9
00:00:23,745 --> 00:00:25,265
Khobfa, hurry up.

10
00:00:25,345 --> 00:00:28,225
Come on, stand in the middle.
That's right.

11
00:00:28,305 --> 00:00:30,185
One, two…

12
00:00:30,265 --> 00:00:32,745
Whoa, you look like a statue.

13
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:34,585
We're not taking an ID photo. Hold this.

14
00:00:35,905 --> 00:00:37,705
Yeah, try to look natural.

15
00:00:37,785 --> 00:00:39,105
Do we really need to do it like this?

16
00:00:39,185 --> 00:00:40,505
Of course.

17
00:00:40,585 --> 00:00:42,865
This is a poster
to recruit new band members.

18
00:00:42,945 --> 00:00:45,145
If the photos aren't appealing,
who'll apply?

19
00:00:45,225 --> 00:00:47,625
But I don't like competitions.
I don't like competing.

20
00:00:47,705 --> 00:00:49,425
You don't have to think of it that way.

21
00:00:49,505 --> 00:00:52,105
Just get onstage, play,
and let people hear your music.

22
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:57,345
If no one ever hears a good song,
can it really be called a good song?

23
00:00:57,425 --> 00:00:58,265
Right?

24
00:00:58,345 --> 00:00:59,465
Not necessarily.

25
00:00:59,545 --> 00:01:01,665
There are plenty of great songs
that hardly anyone listens to.

26
00:01:01,745 --> 00:01:04,145
Whatever. Come on.

27
00:01:04,225 --> 00:01:06,025
One, two.

28
00:01:06,105 --> 00:01:07,545
Let's try another pose.

29
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:10,465
Lift the guitar like this.
Rest it on your shoulder.

30
00:01:10,545 --> 00:01:12,025
Yeah, just like that.

31
00:01:12,105 --> 00:01:13,865
And smile.

32
00:01:13,945 --> 00:01:16,505
If you don't smile in this pose,
you'll look intimidating.

33
00:01:16,585 --> 00:01:18,305
Smile.
People might be too scared to apply.

34
00:01:18,385 --> 00:01:20,705
One, two, three.

35
00:01:23,905 --> 00:01:25,425
This one looks great.

36
00:01:25,505 --> 00:01:27,265
Don't you think I'm smiling too much?

37
00:01:29,505 --> 00:01:31,825
Too much? No. It's barely a smile.

38
00:01:32,585 --> 00:01:34,465
Or do you prefer this?

39
00:01:34,545 --> 00:01:35,585
This one's good.

40
00:01:36,185 --> 00:01:38,585
You look like you're mad at someone.

41
00:01:38,665 --> 00:01:41,705
You need to smile like this. Like this.

42
00:01:44,105 --> 00:01:45,785
THE GRANDEST CONTEST OF OUR UNIVERSITY

43
00:01:45,865 --> 00:01:49,705
Do you think anyone will join my band?

44
00:01:51,505 --> 00:01:53,825
Of course. Someone will.

45
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:55,345
And if no one does,

46
00:01:56,505 --> 00:01:58,065
we'll find a way to make it happen.

47
00:02:57,305 --> 00:03:00,705
Hey, people are encouraging us
to form a band for the university contest.

48
00:03:01,305 --> 00:03:04,145
Yeah, one of the seniors asked me
to convince you to enter.

49
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:06,025
He said it'd make
this year's contest more exciting.

50
00:03:08,425 --> 00:03:13,185
That does sound interesting.
If I apply, will you help me?

51
00:03:17,665 --> 00:03:20,745
Try begging me cutely.
Maybe you'll win me over.

52
00:03:28,785 --> 00:03:33,705
Little Mochi, would you please
consider accepting me, Krit?

53
00:03:34,385 --> 00:03:36,185
I'll think about it.

54
00:03:37,785 --> 00:03:38,665
Really?

55
00:03:39,465 --> 00:03:40,665
I don't know.

56
00:03:40,745 --> 00:03:42,985
DAD

57
00:03:48,505 --> 00:03:49,505
I'll be right back.

58
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:03,625
GRANDMA

59
00:04:08,705 --> 00:04:09,785
GRANDMA

60
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:17,265
GRANDMA

61
00:04:23,945 --> 00:04:27,025
Your grandma called you so many times.
Are you really not going to answer?

62
00:04:47,265 --> 00:04:48,145
Hi, Grandma.

63
00:04:48,225 --> 00:04:51,705
Khobfa, how have you been?
Are you doing okay?

64
00:04:52,305 --> 00:04:54,265
Come visit me this weekend, dear.

65
00:04:54,345 --> 00:04:57,905
I'll probably be busy with work.

66
00:04:57,985 --> 00:04:59,665
Really?

67
00:05:00,225 --> 00:05:03,185
You can bring your work and do it here.
I miss you.

68
00:05:03,785 --> 00:05:04,905
I also…

69
00:05:07,465 --> 00:05:10,865
If I finish my work, I'll go and see you.

70
00:05:10,945 --> 00:05:13,585
All right. I'll be waiting.

71
00:05:13,665 --> 00:05:14,585
Okay.

72
00:05:18,465 --> 00:05:20,625
Come on.
Let's continue checking our photos.

73
00:05:23,385 --> 00:05:24,985
Let me take a break for a while.

74
00:05:41,345 --> 00:05:43,665
My dad called to remind me
about dinner at home.

75
00:05:44,265 --> 00:05:47,465
But something feels strange this time.

76
00:05:48,225 --> 00:05:51,825
What's strange about it?
It's a good thing your dad called.

77
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:56,585
He told me to invite you too.

78
00:06:16,385 --> 00:06:21,465
This is the plant you told me
you brought from your grandma's, right?

79
00:06:23,465 --> 00:06:24,305
Yeah.

80
00:06:27,745 --> 00:06:31,425
No wonder you take such good care of it.

81
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:41,945
If you miss your grandma,
why don't you go see her?

82
00:06:47,465 --> 00:06:48,505
I think…

83
00:06:49,865 --> 00:06:54,425
she deserves to know
how much you miss her.

84
00:07:01,025 --> 00:07:02,065
You too.

85
00:07:07,225 --> 00:07:09,345
You have every right to miss her too.

86
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,665
But I'm scared.

87
00:07:15,345 --> 00:07:16,545
I'm really scared.

88
00:07:24,025 --> 00:07:27,105
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA
MAR 6, 1980-JAN 12, 2020

89
00:07:35,065 --> 00:07:37,385
Have you decided
where you're going to live?

90
00:07:38,785 --> 00:07:39,905
What do you mean?

91
00:07:40,425 --> 00:07:41,865
You got accepted, didn't you?

92
00:07:43,025 --> 00:07:44,985
Move somewhere near campus and…

93
00:07:46,225 --> 00:07:47,865
Just don't come back here.

94
00:07:49,145 --> 00:07:50,425
What do you mean?

95
00:07:53,985 --> 00:07:58,265
Do you want Grandma to die
like your parents did?

96
00:08:03,545 --> 00:08:04,865
You're bad luck.

97
00:08:04,945 --> 00:08:06,945
Everyone around you ends up suffering.

98
00:08:07,025 --> 00:08:08,625
The fortune teller warned us about you.

99
00:08:08,705 --> 00:08:10,585
But Mom and Dad said that wasn't true.

100
00:08:10,665 --> 00:08:11,865
Then where are they now?

101
00:08:13,465 --> 00:08:14,505
Where are they, huh?

102
00:08:14,585 --> 00:08:16,265
If it weren't for you?

103
00:08:19,585 --> 00:08:20,785
I'm sorry.

104
00:08:22,665 --> 00:08:23,545
I…

105
00:08:23,625 --> 00:08:28,385
If you really love Grandma,
don't ever come back to see her.

106
00:08:28,465 --> 00:08:29,905
Do you understand?

107
00:08:50,145 --> 00:08:51,385
I knew it.

108
00:08:52,465 --> 00:08:55,665
Someone as kind as you
must have reasons for doing anything.

109
00:08:58,025 --> 00:09:00,145
But your uncle
deserves a punch in the face.

110
00:09:00,225 --> 00:09:01,985
No, a hundred punches.

111
00:09:02,065 --> 00:09:03,585
Right in the face!

112
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:05,465
Gosh.

113
00:09:10,185 --> 00:09:14,425
You once told me that,
whenever I'm by your side,

114
00:09:14,985 --> 00:09:16,945
everything will work out, right?

115
00:09:18,785 --> 00:09:21,585
Yeah. Why?

116
00:09:25,225 --> 00:09:29,505
Then let's go see your grandma together.

117
00:09:48,705 --> 00:09:50,905
Grandma, I'm here!

118
00:09:53,305 --> 00:09:54,785
Khobfa!

119
00:10:10,625 --> 00:10:13,065
How do I look?

120
00:10:14,465 --> 00:10:16,305
You look good.

121
00:10:17,425 --> 00:10:18,665
I'm not confident at all.

122
00:10:18,745 --> 00:10:21,025
I've never met your family before.

123
00:10:23,625 --> 00:10:25,385
I'm sure it'll be fine.

124
00:10:25,985 --> 00:10:27,345
Dad just wants to get to know you.

125
00:10:28,185 --> 00:10:30,985
Have you ever brought anyone
to meet your dad before?

126
00:10:31,065 --> 00:10:32,905
No. You're the first.

127
00:10:32,985 --> 00:10:34,105
Really?

128
00:10:34,185 --> 00:10:37,545
You're the first person
he's ever asked me to bring home.

129
00:10:38,625 --> 00:10:39,985
I'm nervous.

130
00:10:40,065 --> 00:10:44,905
What do you think your dad will ask me?

131
00:10:50,105 --> 00:10:51,185
What's your name?

132
00:10:52,705 --> 00:10:54,385
My name is Rin.

133
00:10:54,465 --> 00:10:57,185
What's your relationship with Khobfa?

134
00:11:02,505 --> 00:11:03,425
Right now, we're--

135
00:11:03,505 --> 00:11:05,745
-We're roommates.
-Ouch!

136
00:11:05,825 --> 00:11:07,385
Yeah, just roommates.

137
00:11:07,465 --> 00:11:11,865
I just learned that kids these days
call their partners "roommates."

138
00:11:12,945 --> 00:11:16,585
No, ma'am. We're not dating. We're not.

139
00:11:18,265 --> 00:11:22,025
We're in the talking stage,
but we're not together yet.

140
00:11:23,905 --> 00:11:25,305
Then keep talking.

141
00:11:25,385 --> 00:11:31,145
Talk while walking,
standing, or lying down.

142
00:11:31,225 --> 00:11:35,065
Keep it up,
and Rin will eventually give in.

143
00:11:41,225 --> 00:11:44,105
-Will you really give in?
-What?

144
00:11:46,665 --> 00:11:49,465
I haven't seen Khobfa smile like this
in a very long time.

145
00:11:50,345 --> 00:11:54,105
You must be the one who makes him smile.

146
00:11:56,385 --> 00:11:57,345
Me?

147
00:12:10,345 --> 00:12:11,425
Yes.

148
00:12:11,505 --> 00:12:13,625
I was the one
who asked Krit to invite you.

149
00:12:20,025 --> 00:12:23,345
Oh, thank you for inviting me.

150
00:12:23,425 --> 00:12:26,345
Is there something
you wanted to discuss with me?

151
00:12:27,065 --> 00:12:28,465
Nothing.

152
00:12:29,065 --> 00:12:32,665
We just wanted to meet someone
our son is close to.

153
00:12:33,465 --> 00:12:34,425
Right, honey?

154
00:12:35,025 --> 00:12:36,025
Yes.

155
00:12:36,105 --> 00:12:38,625
It's nice to finally meet you in person.

156
00:12:39,185 --> 00:12:43,345
Until now, we had only seen you
in the clips Kong and Kan showed us.

157
00:12:43,425 --> 00:12:45,545
What clips?

158
00:12:47,465 --> 00:12:50,505
The clips from your campaign.

159
00:12:51,105 --> 00:12:52,345
Oh, right.

160
00:12:52,865 --> 00:12:57,025
We're running a campaign
to promote the university's image.

161
00:12:57,105 --> 00:13:00,625
We also have a joint channel now
with over 100,000 followers.

162
00:13:00,705 --> 00:13:02,065
Well…

163
00:13:02,145 --> 00:13:03,665
That sounds interesting.

164
00:13:08,585 --> 00:13:11,105
How long have you been living with Mochi?

165
00:13:15,745 --> 00:13:17,385
It's been two years
since my dad passed away.

166
00:13:17,985 --> 00:13:19,465
These are my parents.

167
00:13:25,825 --> 00:13:28,105
Everyone in your family is good-looking.

168
00:13:29,345 --> 00:13:30,225
Of course.

169
00:13:31,425 --> 00:13:33,625
What? I was complimenting your parents.

170
00:13:34,625 --> 00:13:36,865
Complimenting them
is basically complimenting me.

171
00:13:38,465 --> 00:13:41,505
Mom, Dad, this is my future boyfriend.

172
00:13:43,185 --> 00:13:45,105
What? You've gone too far.

173
00:13:45,785 --> 00:13:50,505
Sir, ma'am, we'll see how it goes.
It'll probably take a long time.

174
00:13:50,585 --> 00:13:52,345
-Not long.
-A long time.

175
00:13:52,425 --> 00:13:54,025
-Not long.
-A long time.

176
00:13:54,105 --> 00:13:54,945
No, it won't.

177
00:13:55,785 --> 00:13:57,265
Hey!

178
00:14:00,065 --> 00:14:03,305
Well, your room is pretty nice.

179
00:14:07,265 --> 00:14:08,505
Whoa.

180
00:14:29,625 --> 00:14:32,225
I DON'T WANT TO GO TO SCHOOL.
WHY DOESN'T ANYONE LIKE ME?

181
00:14:32,305 --> 00:14:33,785
WHY DOES EVERYONE HAVE TO HATE ME?

182
00:14:37,105 --> 00:14:39,105
I don't want to be a jinx.

183
00:14:39,185 --> 00:14:40,665
I don't want to be a jinx.

184
00:14:40,745 --> 00:14:42,185
I don't want to be a jinx.

185
00:14:42,265 --> 00:14:43,865
I don't want to be a jinx.

186
00:14:43,945 --> 00:14:48,345
I don't want to be a jinx!

187
00:14:54,985 --> 00:14:58,305
Mom and Dad said I was their gift.

188
00:15:04,745 --> 00:15:05,785
Here you go.

189
00:15:14,505 --> 00:15:15,505
This one's for you.

190
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:20,465
Thank you.

191
00:15:23,985 --> 00:15:25,145
This is for me?

192
00:15:25,225 --> 00:15:26,785
Of course.

193
00:15:26,865 --> 00:15:31,465
I invited you to dinner with my family,
so of course I got you a gift.

194
00:15:32,585 --> 00:15:33,585
Thank you.

195
00:16:00,945 --> 00:16:05,345
Krit, Kong, Kan,
could you get my things from upstairs?

196
00:16:08,505 --> 00:16:09,385
Sure.

197
00:16:12,465 --> 00:16:13,505
You don't have to go.

198
00:16:14,945 --> 00:16:16,345
Let the three of them go.

199
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:20,545
Stay and keep us company.

200
00:16:29,465 --> 00:16:31,385
Of course, Grandma. Don't worry.

201
00:16:31,465 --> 00:16:33,465
I'll shape them as well as I can.

202
00:16:34,465 --> 00:16:35,825
Let me see.

203
00:16:35,905 --> 00:16:37,625
Here, Grandma. Look.

204
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,585
You're good at this.

205
00:16:40,785 --> 00:16:43,825
Grandma, should I put them in these bowls?

206
00:16:43,905 --> 00:16:46,065
Yes. Pick the pretty ones.

207
00:16:46,145 --> 00:16:47,185
Okay.

208
00:16:51,665 --> 00:16:55,825
Thank you, Rin,
for bringing Khobfa back to see me.

209
00:16:56,945 --> 00:17:00,345
It wasn't me.
Khobfa already wanted to visit you.

210
00:17:00,425 --> 00:17:02,505
If you hadn't come…

211
00:17:04,505 --> 00:17:06,345
he wouldn't have.

212
00:17:07,065 --> 00:17:09,545
Khobfa has a hard time trusting people.

213
00:17:10,145 --> 00:17:12,385
He had a bad experience at school,

214
00:17:12,985 --> 00:17:16,665
so he quit basketball
and music altogether.

215
00:17:18,665 --> 00:17:20,825
Khobfa used to be in a band?

216
00:17:21,785 --> 00:17:22,785
Yes.

217
00:17:25,944 --> 00:17:27,145
I see.

218
00:17:32,625 --> 00:17:36,665
There's still so much about Khobfa
that I don't know.

219
00:17:42,425 --> 00:17:45,105
I've got it, Dad. Where should I put it?

220
00:17:48,665 --> 00:17:51,465
I have somewhere else to be,
so I'll excuse myself.

221
00:17:52,385 --> 00:17:53,865
Goodbye.

222
00:18:09,865 --> 00:18:12,425
Influencers sure are busy, aren't they?

223
00:18:13,185 --> 00:18:16,185
Let him go. It's actually better.

224
00:18:16,265 --> 00:18:18,185
Now it's just our family.

225
00:18:18,265 --> 00:18:20,105
Come on. Let's eat.

226
00:18:27,105 --> 00:18:32,145
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA 1980-2020
NITTAYA CHAIPANHA 1980-2016

227
00:18:34,105 --> 00:18:37,745
Sweet rice balls with egg.
Grandma and I made them for you.

228
00:18:42,585 --> 00:18:43,985
Rin helped too.

229
00:18:46,705 --> 00:18:50,385
Mom, Dad, please watch over Grandma.

230
00:18:54,785 --> 00:18:56,945
Your parents are in heaven.

231
00:18:57,025 --> 00:18:58,865
Don't bother them.

232
00:18:58,945 --> 00:19:01,505
You're the one
who has to care for your grandma.

233
00:19:02,665 --> 00:19:03,625
But I'm a jinx--

234
00:19:03,705 --> 00:19:04,745
A gift.

235
00:19:06,185 --> 00:19:10,545
You're your parents' gift,
just like you wrote in your diary.

236
00:19:18,065 --> 00:19:20,625
I'm sorry. I happened to come across it.

237
00:19:28,745 --> 00:19:33,025
But I'm sure your parents
felt the same way.

238
00:19:49,545 --> 00:19:51,265
You've got it easy.

239
00:19:51,345 --> 00:19:53,545
You made me pedal all the way here.
Now I have to pedal back.

240
00:19:53,625 --> 00:19:56,265
I don't know how to ride a bike.

241
00:19:56,345 --> 00:19:58,265
You can ride a motorcycle, though.

242
00:19:58,345 --> 00:20:01,305
You rode on the back of mine,
and now I'm riding on the back of yours.

243
00:20:01,385 --> 00:20:02,905
That makes us even, right?

244
00:20:02,985 --> 00:20:03,985
Hey, Rin.

245
00:20:04,545 --> 00:20:05,385
What?

246
00:20:08,745 --> 00:20:09,705
It's raining.

247
00:20:10,865 --> 00:20:12,905
So? What's there to be afraid of?

248
00:20:12,985 --> 00:20:14,185
Shouldn't we find shelter?

249
00:20:15,465 --> 00:20:17,545
Didn't you ever play in the rain as a kid?

250
00:20:17,625 --> 00:20:18,865
It's so much fun.

251
00:20:19,745 --> 00:20:20,905
Should we find shelter?

252
00:20:20,985 --> 00:20:23,785
No. Let's play in the rain. It's fun.

253
00:20:24,505 --> 00:20:27,145
Come on, lift your feet! Quick!

254
00:20:27,225 --> 00:20:28,545
Rin! What the hell are you doing?

255
00:20:28,625 --> 00:20:30,625
I told you.
Playing in the rain is awesome.

256
00:20:30,705 --> 00:20:31,745
Hey!

257
00:20:35,825 --> 00:20:37,305
This really is fun.

258
00:20:39,145 --> 00:20:40,105
Yeah!

259
00:20:56,545 --> 00:20:57,425
Hey.

260
00:20:57,505 --> 00:20:59,425
Why don't you go change in the bathroom?

261
00:21:06,585 --> 00:21:09,185
Why? Are you shy?

262
00:21:10,625 --> 00:21:11,945
Come here. I'll take it off for you.

263
00:21:12,025 --> 00:21:13,145
Hey, no need.

264
00:21:16,465 --> 00:21:17,865
I can do it myself.

265
00:21:56,145 --> 00:21:57,665
Do you want to shower with me?

266
00:22:16,825 --> 00:22:17,985
Why are you here again?

267
00:22:18,065 --> 00:22:19,705
Get out right now!

268
00:22:19,785 --> 00:22:22,945
This is my house. What right do you have
to give it to Khobfa?

269
00:22:26,145 --> 00:22:27,305
Khobfa! Where are you?

270
00:22:27,385 --> 00:22:28,865
If I don't leave it to Khobfa,

271
00:22:28,945 --> 00:22:30,425
then should I leave it to you?

272
00:22:30,505 --> 00:22:34,865
You never cared about me all these years.
Why come making demands now?

273
00:22:34,945 --> 00:22:37,545
Go. Get out!

274
00:22:37,625 --> 00:22:40,665
You care more about your grandson
than you do your own son?

275
00:22:42,345 --> 00:22:44,385
Have you gone senile?

276
00:22:44,465 --> 00:22:46,425
Grandma is your mother too.

277
00:22:47,545 --> 00:22:48,625
Show her some respect.

278
00:22:49,225 --> 00:22:50,545
Who are you to lecture me?

279
00:22:51,145 --> 00:22:53,705
I'm not lecturing you.
I'm just warning you.

280
00:22:53,785 --> 00:22:56,705
I warned you not to come back, didn't I?

281
00:22:57,305 --> 00:22:59,905
What happened last time?
Grandma ended up in the hospital.

282
00:22:59,985 --> 00:23:01,265
It was because of you.

283
00:23:06,785 --> 00:23:10,985
Grandma calls me to visit all the time.
I can't bring myself to say no to her.

284
00:23:11,065 --> 00:23:12,465
You can't say no,

285
00:23:13,385 --> 00:23:15,145
or are you hoping to get something?

286
00:23:16,505 --> 00:23:17,705
Like you, Uncle?

287
00:23:20,105 --> 00:23:21,825
How dare you speak to me like that?

288
00:23:21,905 --> 00:23:24,305
Don't bring bad luck to my mom
like you did to your parents.

289
00:23:24,385 --> 00:23:25,465
Stop it right now!

290
00:23:25,545 --> 00:23:26,505
Isn't it true, Mom?

291
00:23:26,585 --> 00:23:28,265
Everyone knows this kid is a jinx.

292
00:23:35,585 --> 00:23:36,745
What?

293
00:23:36,825 --> 00:23:38,625
You want to punch me, you little shit?

294
00:23:38,705 --> 00:23:39,585
That's enough!

295
00:23:39,665 --> 00:23:43,785
What kind of adult
keeps reopening a kid's wounds like this?

296
00:23:43,865 --> 00:23:47,425
Oh, so you're Khobfa's friend.

297
00:23:48,585 --> 00:23:51,345
No wonder. You're both pieces of shit.

298
00:23:53,545 --> 00:23:56,905
If you're this drunk, go home. Go!

299
00:23:56,985 --> 00:23:58,305
Mind your fucking business!

300
00:24:06,265 --> 00:24:07,105
Hey!

301
00:24:07,185 --> 00:24:09,105
Don't you dare touch my man.

302
00:24:10,345 --> 00:24:11,865
Let go of me!

303
00:24:11,945 --> 00:24:13,425
That hurts!

304
00:24:13,505 --> 00:24:15,545
Khobfa, that's enough.

305
00:24:27,825 --> 00:24:29,185
I'll go now, Grandma.

306
00:24:30,625 --> 00:24:32,545
Khobfa!

307
00:24:32,625 --> 00:24:34,185
Go wherever the hell you want, bastard.

308
00:24:34,265 --> 00:24:35,865
-Khobfa, come back!
-Don't ever come back!

309
00:24:36,465 --> 00:24:40,025
Khobfa, how long will you keep
running away from your problems?

310
00:24:41,425 --> 00:24:44,545
Seriously, how long will you let people
look down on you like this?

311
00:24:45,305 --> 00:24:47,345
That's because I really am a jinx!

312
00:24:48,985 --> 00:24:51,065
Listen to me.

313
00:24:51,625 --> 00:24:53,305
You haven't had any bad luck at all.

314
00:24:53,905 --> 00:24:55,785
You haven't done anything wrong.

315
00:24:57,145 --> 00:24:59,185
You're not me. What would you know?

316
00:25:00,985 --> 00:25:02,385
Why wouldn't I know?

317
00:25:06,945 --> 00:25:08,945
Because you're lucky.

318
00:25:09,025 --> 00:25:11,225
Everyone loves and admires you.

319
00:25:11,305 --> 00:25:13,225
You weren't born a jinx like me!

320
00:25:13,305 --> 00:25:16,265
You think I've never had bad luck, huh?

321
00:25:18,025 --> 00:25:21,065
Mom, I won another award.
I'll bring it home to show you.

322
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:23,425
-Don't run, sweetie. You'll fall.
-Dad!

323
00:25:23,505 --> 00:25:24,785
-Hurry.
-Walk slowly.

324
00:25:24,865 --> 00:25:26,225
What do you want to play?

325
00:25:26,305 --> 00:25:29,305
You think someone who was lied to
his whole life about his dad being dead,

326
00:25:29,385 --> 00:25:32,185
only to learn he'd run off
to start a happier family,

327
00:25:32,265 --> 00:25:34,705
leaving his wife and son behind
with this stupid curse…

328
00:25:39,625 --> 00:25:42,705
You think that's what happens
to someone who's lucky?

329
00:25:46,785 --> 00:25:47,825
I'm sorry.

330
00:25:54,305 --> 00:25:55,265
Forget it.

331
00:25:57,785 --> 00:25:59,225
It's good to let it out.

332
00:26:00,305 --> 00:26:01,705
The same goes for you.

333
00:26:02,385 --> 00:26:04,105
You should let it out sometimes.

334
00:26:05,265 --> 00:26:06,985
Why do you keep bottling it all up?

335
00:26:08,345 --> 00:26:12,305
Are you crazy? I'm a person, not a robot.

336
00:26:12,385 --> 00:26:14,305
I can't flip an emotion switch
like you can.

337
00:26:15,425 --> 00:26:18,785
You can. You really can.

338
00:26:22,425 --> 00:26:23,745
I can't do it.

339
00:26:28,625 --> 00:26:29,945
I know what to do.

340
00:26:30,545 --> 00:26:32,745
I'll take you somewhere
to blow off some steam.

341
00:26:33,745 --> 00:26:34,865
What?

342
00:26:43,545 --> 00:26:44,745
That's more like it.

343
00:26:44,825 --> 00:26:46,785
Come on. I'll take you there.

344
00:26:59,185 --> 00:27:04,145
Okay, now that we're ready, pick one.

345
00:27:04,785 --> 00:27:05,865
Which one?

346
00:27:08,705 --> 00:27:10,145
Here. Let's go with this one.

347
00:27:11,905 --> 00:27:14,665
Now dip it into any color.

348
00:27:14,745 --> 00:27:18,625
Think about the awful thing
that just happened,

349
00:27:18,705 --> 00:27:20,865
then splash it onto this.

350
00:27:23,665 --> 00:27:25,225
Here, I'll show you.

351
00:27:32,345 --> 00:27:35,425
Just let it all out.

352
00:27:35,505 --> 00:27:39,065
Everything bad, everything awful,
let it all out on here.

353
00:27:40,505 --> 00:27:41,385
Give it a try.

354
00:27:51,025 --> 00:27:53,505
I'm not a jinx.
I didn't do anything wrong.

355
00:27:53,585 --> 00:27:55,745
I'm not a jinx.
I didn't do anything wrong.

356
00:27:55,825 --> 00:27:57,985
I'm not a jinx!
I didn't do anything wrong!

357
00:27:58,065 --> 00:27:59,185
Yeah, that's it.

358
00:27:59,265 --> 00:28:00,825
Just like that.

359
00:28:01,425 --> 00:28:02,585
Now that's Khobfa!

360
00:28:02,665 --> 00:28:03,705
Now that's Rin!

361
00:28:07,265 --> 00:28:08,785
Khobfa!

362
00:28:08,865 --> 00:28:12,105
-Hey, relax!
-You're covered in green!

363
00:28:12,185 --> 00:28:13,505
Hey!

364
00:28:14,065 --> 00:28:15,105
Whoa!

365
00:28:21,585 --> 00:28:24,585
Yes. Krit and I have been friends
since high school.

366
00:28:25,985 --> 00:28:28,385
But you only recently started
making couple content together?

367
00:28:28,985 --> 00:28:30,105
Yes.

368
00:28:36,545 --> 00:28:38,585
I do support talented kids…

369
00:28:39,185 --> 00:28:43,385
from ordinary backgrounds.

370
00:28:46,025 --> 00:28:50,865
But honestly, this whole
couple-content thing you're doing

371
00:28:50,945 --> 00:28:52,385
isn't going to work.

372
00:28:53,665 --> 00:28:54,745
You should stop.

373
00:28:56,185 --> 00:28:57,025
But Krit and I--

374
00:28:57,105 --> 00:28:58,665
I've had someone look into you.

375
00:28:59,185 --> 00:29:01,385
You grew up in an orphanage, didn't you?

376
00:29:01,465 --> 00:29:05,105
Money must be important to you.

377
00:29:05,185 --> 00:29:08,305
Name your price, and I'll pay it.

378
00:29:08,385 --> 00:29:10,625
But you have to stay away from my son.

379
00:29:18,905 --> 00:29:20,265
I've got it, Dad.

380
00:29:20,345 --> 00:29:21,705
Where should I put it?

381
00:29:47,665 --> 00:29:49,745
What made you call me here today?

382
00:29:51,465 --> 00:29:52,945
I just wanted to see you.

383
00:29:54,745 --> 00:29:56,385
Don't you have a boyfriend?

384
00:29:57,465 --> 00:29:58,585
Or did you get dumped?

385
00:30:00,985 --> 00:30:02,145
I'm single.

386
00:30:02,705 --> 00:30:06,625
We're just in the talking stage.

387
00:30:10,705 --> 00:30:11,945
So…

388
00:30:14,185 --> 00:30:16,025
I still have a chance tonight, right?

389
00:30:20,625 --> 00:30:22,065
KRIT

390
00:30:44,145 --> 00:30:48,665
Hey, Krit. Weren't you going to a bar?
I thought you were with Mochi.

391
00:30:49,185 --> 00:30:50,665
What bar?

392
00:30:50,745 --> 00:30:54,585
Mochi posted a story.
I saw it and thought it was your hand.

393
00:30:57,185 --> 00:30:58,065
Look.

394
00:31:04,705 --> 00:31:06,545
I think Mochi hid his story from you.

395
00:31:11,225 --> 00:31:12,065
Huh?

396
00:31:15,705 --> 00:31:17,865
MS. DARAN

397
00:31:20,185 --> 00:31:21,145
Rin.

398
00:31:21,905 --> 00:31:22,745
Rin.

399
00:31:22,825 --> 00:31:23,745
Yeah?

400
00:31:23,825 --> 00:31:25,025
Someone's calling you.

401
00:31:25,105 --> 00:31:26,585
Who is it?

402
00:31:28,105 --> 00:31:29,505
Ms. Daran.

403
00:31:29,585 --> 00:31:31,105
Oh, really?

404
00:31:31,185 --> 00:31:32,785
-Yeah.
-Okay.

405
00:31:42,545 --> 00:31:44,185
Hello, Mom.

406
00:31:44,785 --> 00:31:46,025
Hello, Rin.

407
00:31:48,585 --> 00:31:51,065
How are you, son?
Did you move to a new place?

408
00:31:51,145 --> 00:31:52,945
Who are you living with?

409
00:31:53,665 --> 00:31:55,065
With Khobfa, Mom.

410
00:31:55,145 --> 00:31:57,905
Really? Can you trust him?

411
00:31:57,985 --> 00:32:00,265
Why aren't you staying with Danthai?

412
00:32:00,345 --> 00:32:02,785
Did something happen between you two?

413
00:32:02,865 --> 00:32:05,865
Whoa, which question
should I answer first, Mom?

414
00:32:05,945 --> 00:32:08,505
Nothing happened between Dan and me.

415
00:32:08,585 --> 00:32:13,345
And as for Khobfa,
I trust him more than anyone.

416
00:32:13,425 --> 00:32:16,545
Is that so? Okay, that's great.

417
00:32:16,625 --> 00:32:20,825
The next time I'm back in Thailand,
don't forget to introduce him to me.

418
00:32:22,625 --> 00:32:24,905
Take care of yourself, okay?

419
00:32:24,985 --> 00:32:26,425
Wait, Mom.

420
00:32:27,745 --> 00:32:29,745
Yes? What is it?

421
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:35,025
Nothing.

422
00:32:38,745 --> 00:32:39,865
Thank you

423
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,625
for being the kind of mother you are.

424
00:32:44,425 --> 00:32:48,665
Hey, what's this?
Why are you suddenly getting sentimental?

425
00:33:03,545 --> 00:33:05,105
I love you, Rin.

426
00:33:07,705 --> 00:33:09,105
I love you too, Mom.

427
00:33:10,425 --> 00:33:12,105
More than anyone in the world.

428
00:33:51,825 --> 00:33:53,705
My mom wants to meet you too.

429
00:33:54,305 --> 00:33:55,545
Really?

430
00:33:55,625 --> 00:33:56,545
Yeah.

431
00:33:57,305 --> 00:33:59,065
I want to meet her too.

432
00:33:59,705 --> 00:34:02,545
Maybe I can ask you
to be my boyfriend in front of her.

433
00:34:03,745 --> 00:34:05,105
Whoa, that's too much.

434
00:34:05,705 --> 00:34:07,345
Boyfriend?

435
00:34:08,065 --> 00:34:10,065
Let's see how things go first.

436
00:34:10,985 --> 00:34:15,145
Stop making that face. Forget it.

437
00:34:44,304 --> 00:34:47,304
I'm glad you opened up to me.

438
00:35:08,385 --> 00:35:09,265
Hey!

439
00:35:22,705 --> 00:35:24,425
What the hell are you two doing?

440
00:35:25,465 --> 00:35:27,065
Stay away from my boyfriend.

441
00:35:35,065 --> 00:35:36,305
We need to talk.

442
00:35:40,945 --> 00:35:42,425
What the hell are you doing?

443
00:35:42,505 --> 00:35:44,105
That's what I should ask you.

444
00:35:44,185 --> 00:35:47,065
You've been avoiding me and lying to me.

445
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:48,665
Why did you do that?

446
00:35:49,345 --> 00:35:51,105
What I do is none of your business.

447
00:35:51,185 --> 00:35:54,265
Don't forget we're just friends
with benefits. I'm not your boyfriend.

448
00:35:54,345 --> 00:35:55,465
I'm worried about you.

449
00:35:57,665 --> 00:36:01,105
You're acting like this
because of my dad, aren't you?

450
00:36:02,105 --> 00:36:03,945
He told you to stop seeing me, didn't he?

451
00:36:06,465 --> 00:36:07,305
Krit.

452
00:36:09,105 --> 00:36:10,505
I know everything.

453
00:36:12,745 --> 00:36:13,985
Who are you calling?

454
00:36:17,265 --> 00:36:20,265
Mochi. He won't answer.

455
00:36:22,465 --> 00:36:23,505
Krit,

456
00:36:24,545 --> 00:36:26,625
Dad asked you and Mochi to come today

457
00:36:27,385 --> 00:36:30,985
because he wanted Mochi
to stop seeing you.

458
00:36:39,145 --> 00:36:42,385
Didn't I tell you to tell me
if anything happened?

459
00:36:44,865 --> 00:36:46,945
I didn't want you
to have problems with your dad.

460
00:36:55,545 --> 00:36:56,625
Hello, Dad.

461
00:36:59,185 --> 00:37:01,745
You said you wanted all your children
to be happy, right?

462
00:37:03,905 --> 00:37:06,905
Well, Mochi and I are so damn happy.

463
00:37:08,705 --> 00:37:11,385
We're not going to break up
because of what you said.

464
00:37:13,945 --> 00:37:15,385
What the fuck are you doing?

465
00:37:16,105 --> 00:37:19,705
You'll get into another fight
with your dad and end up hurt again.

466
00:37:24,585 --> 00:37:28,225
I'd be more hurt if I lost you.

467
00:37:56,665 --> 00:37:59,305
Do you really think
anyone will want to join our band?

468
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:01,265
Someone will.

469
00:38:01,345 --> 00:38:02,865
Look, I put up a new poster.

470
00:38:02,945 --> 00:38:04,905
Your application form is ready too.

471
00:38:05,545 --> 00:38:07,065
Just wait. Someone will show up.

472
00:38:07,145 --> 00:38:09,505
-But will this poster even help--
-Stop.

473
00:38:09,585 --> 00:38:13,105
Whatever you're thinking, don't say it.

474
00:38:16,105 --> 00:38:17,425
Have some faith.

475
00:38:18,025 --> 00:38:19,825
Hey, look. Excuse me!

476
00:38:19,905 --> 00:38:21,865
Are you interested in joining a band?

477
00:38:23,025 --> 00:38:24,105
No, thanks.

478
00:38:28,345 --> 00:38:30,465
THE CAMPUS STAGE
BATTLE OF THE BANDS APPLICATION

479
00:38:31,225 --> 00:38:33,905
It's okay.
There are plenty of people around here.

480
00:38:40,385 --> 00:38:42,945
Don't tell me
you're actually competing in this too.

481
00:38:45,785 --> 00:38:46,985
Let's go, Khobfa.

482
00:38:48,025 --> 00:38:49,785
There's still time to withdraw.

483
00:38:49,865 --> 00:38:50,705
Yeah.

484
00:38:50,785 --> 00:38:53,865
If you don't have a band,
you can't compete.

485
00:38:53,945 --> 00:38:56,825
I don't have one yet, but I will.

486
00:38:56,905 --> 00:38:58,585
Don't worry about losing so soon.

487
00:38:59,385 --> 00:39:02,465
Really? Well, good luck.

488
00:39:07,185 --> 00:39:08,865
Krit! Mochi!

489
00:39:08,945 --> 00:39:10,505
I'm interested. Where do I sign up?

490
00:39:10,585 --> 00:39:11,545
Right here.

491
00:39:12,865 --> 00:39:14,225
Move!

492
00:39:15,105 --> 00:39:16,185
Scan it now.

493
00:39:18,025 --> 00:39:20,105
-Done.
-Nice.

494
00:39:20,185 --> 00:39:21,465
Hurry.

495
00:39:24,145 --> 00:39:25,985
Hey, guys.

496
00:39:26,545 --> 00:39:27,585
What are you doing?

497
00:39:31,025 --> 00:39:32,625
HORIZON IS LOOKING FOR BAND MEMBERS

498
00:39:32,705 --> 00:39:36,065
Shit. Don't tell me you two
are entering the music contest.

499
00:39:36,145 --> 00:39:38,305
You guys came at the perfect time.

500
00:39:38,385 --> 00:39:40,785
Here. Where are your phones?
Join my band right now.

501
00:39:41,385 --> 00:39:43,105
No. No, buddy. No.

502
00:39:43,665 --> 00:39:47,825
You should find someone else.
Don't let us drag you down.

503
00:39:47,905 --> 00:39:49,465
Jinnie's right.

504
00:39:49,545 --> 00:39:51,465
We'd better stick to drawing.

505
00:39:51,545 --> 00:39:53,705
We're not good at that stuff.

506
00:39:54,305 --> 00:39:57,105
But don't worry, man. Someone will apply.

507
00:39:57,185 --> 00:40:00,025
-You two are both handsome.
-Good luck. See you.

508
00:40:07,065 --> 00:40:07,985
Excuse me.

509
00:40:08,065 --> 00:40:11,265
-Hey. Are you here to apply for the band?
-Yes.

510
00:40:11,345 --> 00:40:13,545
-Here. Fill this out.
-There!

511
00:40:16,265 --> 00:40:19,225
I found them. Krit and Mochi. Thank you.

512
00:40:28,145 --> 00:40:29,225
Jeez!

513
00:40:30,545 --> 00:40:32,705
Do you think anyone will actually apply?

514
00:40:37,465 --> 00:40:39,825
Okay, then let's try this.

515
00:40:41,225 --> 00:40:44,585
If we can't find applicants ourselves,
we'll have to rely on the universe.

516
00:40:48,265 --> 00:40:49,305
How?

517
00:40:54,345 --> 00:40:56,745
"A moonlight-bathing ritual
to ward off bad luck."

518
00:40:56,825 --> 00:40:59,505
Now, who wrote this?

519
00:41:01,585 --> 00:41:02,705
MOONLIGHT-BATHING RITUAL

520
00:41:02,785 --> 00:41:03,785
Hey!

521
00:41:04,305 --> 00:41:05,265
Where did you get that?

522
00:41:09,465 --> 00:41:12,145
Moonlight-bathing ritual
to ward off bad luck.

523
00:41:14,705 --> 00:41:16,185
I'm too scared to try it.

524
00:41:16,825 --> 00:41:17,945
What should I do?

525
00:41:18,025 --> 00:41:19,745
I don't want Grandma to suffer
because of me again.

526
00:41:24,265 --> 00:41:25,905
Did you ever try it as a kid?

527
00:41:27,025 --> 00:41:28,905
No. I was too scared.

528
00:41:29,665 --> 00:41:30,865
Then it's time to try.

529
00:41:31,505 --> 00:41:34,945
It'll drive away your bad luck, and people
will finally dare to join your band.

530
00:41:35,025 --> 00:41:38,305
You want me to get naked? No way.

531
00:41:41,705 --> 00:41:44,145
Whoa, this is destiny.

532
00:41:44,865 --> 00:41:46,345
It's a full moon tonight.

533
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,825
I think you should try it.

534
00:41:50,145 --> 00:41:51,145
No.

535
00:41:51,225 --> 00:41:53,825
Come on. You'll feel better.

536
00:41:54,465 --> 00:41:57,465
I want you to make it
into the contest too. Please?

537
00:41:58,505 --> 00:41:59,785
-Please.
-How about this?

538
00:41:59,865 --> 00:42:03,025
-You jump, I jump. Deal?
-Huh?

539
00:42:19,665 --> 00:42:21,105
I did some research.

540
00:42:21,985 --> 00:42:26,345
It says we have to bathe in the moonlight
for at least nine minutes.

541
00:42:27,385 --> 00:42:30,385
And while we're at it,
we have to make a wish too.

542
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:31,545
Are you ready?

543
00:42:33,545 --> 00:42:35,025
Fine. Let's do it.

544
00:42:36,225 --> 00:42:37,305
Come on.

545
00:42:37,385 --> 00:42:38,385
-Start!
-Start!

546
00:42:49,505 --> 00:42:50,585
Are you ready?

547
00:42:51,385 --> 00:42:52,225
Yeah.

548
00:42:53,665 --> 00:42:55,265
But don't you dare peek.

549
00:42:55,865 --> 00:42:57,385
Same goes for you.

550
00:42:59,185 --> 00:43:01,905
-Three, two, one.
-Three, two, one.

551
00:43:16,465 --> 00:43:20,425
One, two, three.

552
00:43:20,505 --> 00:43:21,425
Hey, who's up there?

553
00:43:23,345 --> 00:43:24,385
-Shit.
-Shit.

554
00:43:25,785 --> 00:43:27,065
Let's move.

555
00:43:59,505 --> 00:44:01,705
Emergency assembly.
Everyone to the first floor now.

556
00:44:03,785 --> 00:44:04,865
Roger that.

557
00:44:24,825 --> 00:44:26,345
Don't forget to make a wish.

558
00:44:27,385 --> 00:44:28,865
Okay. You lead.

559
00:44:42,545 --> 00:44:45,985
May the moonlight shining down tonight…

560
00:44:46,865 --> 00:44:49,785
"May the moonlight shining down tonight…"

561
00:44:51,345 --> 00:44:54,825
…cleanse Khobfa of every bit of bad luck.

562
00:44:55,425 --> 00:44:58,905
"…cleanse Khobfa
of every bit of bad luck."

563
00:45:02,745 --> 00:45:06,545
And please let the person standing
in front of me become my boyfriend.

564
00:45:43,465 --> 00:45:45,145
These guys are your bandmates?

565
00:45:45,225 --> 00:45:46,425
Can they even play instruments?

566
00:45:46,505 --> 00:45:48,625
Our band members never back down.

567
00:45:48,705 --> 00:45:49,785
No wonder they're your friends.

568
00:45:49,865 --> 00:45:52,065
The competition hasn't even started.
He's so good.

569
00:45:52,145 --> 00:45:53,025
That's so cool.

570
00:45:53,105 --> 00:45:54,625
I'm going all out in the final round.

571
00:45:54,705 --> 00:45:55,705
Same here.

572
00:45:55,785 --> 00:45:57,465
There's no way I'll lose to you.

573
00:45:57,545 --> 00:45:59,825
If I win, will you be my boyfriend?

574
00:45:59,905 --> 00:46:01,665
You've got me cheering you on.

575
00:46:01,745 --> 00:46:03,305
Are you really not going to keep fighting?

576
00:46:03,385 --> 00:46:05,945
Why is the cure for the curse here?

577
00:46:06,025 --> 00:46:08,265
I secretly put our story
into the song too.

578
00:46:08,345 --> 00:46:10,545
My boyfriend really knows
how to fill me with positivity.

579
00:46:10,625 --> 00:46:11,945
Can I kiss you?

